    reg {
        name = "System-on-chip (SoC) clock selection register";
        desc = "PERI_CRG12 is an SoC clock selection register.

Vendor U-Boot (start.S/platform.h `REG_CRG12 0x30`) and the vendor Linux clock driver (clk-hi3518ev20x.c, `sysapb_mux` at 0x30 bit 0) agree with this layout: bus_sc_sel = 0 selects 24 MHz, 1 selects 198 MHz; the system APB clock (UART/timer/GPIO/WDG parent) is that clock divided by 4 (6 MHz or 49.5 MHz).

Mode switching: the data sheet (Table 3-5) knows a Normal mode (ARM clocks from the PLL) and a Slow mode (24 MHz crystal, APLL off), but this chip has no mode field in SYS_CTRL SC_CTRL; the mode is just cpu_sc_sel / bus_sc_sel here, and PERI_CRG55 clk_cpu_seled / clk_bus_seled report when a switch has completed. Change the APLL only with cpu_sc_sel = 0, wait for PERI_CRG58 apll_lock, then set cpu_sc_sel = 1.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG12 (offset 0x30, printed page 3-20, `hi3518ev200-datasheet.txt` line 23241).";

        enum PERI_CRG12_mem_adjust_bypass_enum {
            ADJUSTABLE = 0 { name = "Adjustable"; desc = "adjustable"; };
            NOT_ADJUSTABLE = 1 { name = "Not Adjustable"; desc = "not adjustable"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "mem_adjust_bypass";
            desc = "mem adjustability select";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG12_mem_adjust_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
