    reg {
        name = "USB clock and soft reset control register";
        desc = "PERI_CRG46 is a USB2.0 clock and soft reset control register.

USB 2.0 host/device clock and reset. Reset deassert order (DS 12.7.3): wait >= 10 us, clear usb_phy_port0_treq, clear usb_phy_req, wait 250 us, clear usb_ctrl_utmi0_req, clear usb_hrst_req. The vendor U-Boot driver (hiusb-3518ev200.c, `REG_CRG46 0xb8`) and the vendor U-Boot platform.h use PERI_CRG46 at 0xB8 as the data sheet does; the vendor Linux clock driver (clk-hi3518ev20x.c) uses offset 0xB4 (= PERI_CRG45, undocumented) for `usb2_cttl_utmi0_req` bit 5 and `usb2_hrst_req` bit 0 (see docs/UPSTREAM-PR-NOTES.md); 0xB8 is modelled (data sheet + U-Boot, 2 sources against 1). The vendor U-Boot driver also sets and clears bit 4 (`USB_CTRL_HUB_REG`, a hub/controller reset) although the bit table lists [4:3] as reserved (reset 0); DS 12.7.3 additionally names a `usb_otg_phy_srst_req` that is not in the bit table (probably the same bit 3 or 4; unresolved). Reset: the header total reset value 0xA7 is modelled (clock on, ctrl/phy/bus in reset); the data sheet bit row prints 1 for all of bits 7:0 (0xFF, i.e. also for the reserved bits 6, 4, 3).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG46 (offset 0xB8, printed page 3-31, `hi3518ev200-datasheet.txt` line 23857).";

        enum PERI_CRG46_usb_device_ctrl_srst_req_enum {
