UART clock select: 00 = APB clock, 01 = 24 MHz, 1X = 6 MHz (vendor U-Boot platform.h UART_CKSEL_APB/24M/6M = 0/1/2 << 19; the vendor U-Boot board_init selects 24 MHz; the vendor Linux clock driver registers the same mux {sysapb, 24m, 6m} at 0xE4 bit 19 but with a width of 1 bit, which cannot select the 6 MHz entry: a vendor driver bug, the data sheet 2-bit field is modelled). Reset 01 = 24 MHz. I2C clock select reset: the data sheet total reset value 0x040BF001 has bit 26 set, i.e. i2c_cksel resets to 01 (24 MHz) although the data sheet bit row prints 0 (the header is modelled; no vendor code reads this field, the vendor device tree clocks the I2Cs from sysapb). The vendor clock driver gates SSP0/SSP1 (bits 13/14) and UART0..2 (bits 15..17) here. Bit 2: the data sheet calls it `t_cap soft reset request` in the text and `rtc_srst_req` in the name column (the RTC's temperature-capture block); bits [22:21] and [18] are reserved but RW in the data sheet.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG57 (offset 0xE4, printed page 3-37, `hi3518ev200-datasheet.txt` line 24196).";

